# srcradar CODEOWNERS
#
# Code review assignments. GitHub auto-requests reviews from the listed
# owners when a PR touches a matching path. We keep this minimal —
# only the load-bearing modules get an explicit owner; everything
# else falls back to repo admins / maintainers.
#
# Format: path pattern -> GitHub usernames / team names.
# Last matching pattern wins (GitHub convention).

# Default — falls back to repo maintainers if nothing more specific
# matches. We intentionally do NOT list a single global owner; PRs
# touching cross-cutting concerns (workflows, etc.) should get
# explicit owners via more-specific rules below.

# ---- CI / build / tooling ----
# Workflows, Dependabot config, ruff config — changes here affect
# every contributor; require an explicit maintainer sign-off.
/.github/         @YOUR_GITHUB_HANDLE
/pyproject.toml   @YOUR_GITHUB_HANDLE

# ---- db_align (Go) ----
# The plugin is LOCKED (manual auth gate per modules/public/db_align/CLAUDE.md);
# any change here deserves an explicit review of the ENScan cookie-handling
# implications.
/modules/public/db_align/   @YOUR_GITHUB_HANDLE

# ---- pdtm pipeline (Bash) ----
# The active-recon 4-stage pipeline. Touching scanner.sh / scan.sh /
# pipeline.sh / scope_import.sh changes how assets are enumerated;
/modules/main/pdtm/        @YOUR_GITHUB_HANDLE

# ---- daily cron (Bash + Python) ----
# Diff generation, dashboard, snapshot orchestration — runs at 03:00 daily
# on production deployments.
/modules/main/daily/        @YOUR_GITHUB_HANDLE

# ---- manage (business entry-point) ----
/modules/main/manage/       @YOUR_GITHUB_HANDLE

# ---- ymicp plugin (Python) ----
# Optional plugin; cookie-gated access.
/modules/public/ymicp/      @YOUR_GITHUB_HANDLE

